---
// Hidden landing / sign-up page for the $97 OpenClaw workshop (rung 1 teaser).
// Excluded from the index, RSS, and sitemap; carries noindex/nofollow; not linked from nav.
// See: QBall openclaw-consulting-cold-email → receipts/workshop-signup-page-strategy-2026-09-11/
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';

// ── Easy-to-edit values ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
const CHECKOUT_URL = 'https://buy.stripe.com/7sY149efa5NVa87gsw7AI00';
const SESSION_DATE = 'Saturday, October 10, 2026 · 10:00 AM PT / 1:00 PM ET';
const EARLY_PRICE = '$97';
const FULL_PRICE = '$147';
const SEAT_CAP = 'seats are capped so the review blocks actually work';
const MIN_SEATS = 'The session runs with at least 5 paid seats — if it doesn\'t fill, you get a full refund or a transfer.';
const WEEKDAY_FALLBACK = 'If enough people ask, I\'ll open a weekday cohort.';
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`The 3-Hour OpenClaw Workshop — ${SITE_TITLE}`}
			description="A live, 3-hour working session on the OpenClaw setup I actually run in production. Bring your messiest manual workflow; leave with a named diagnosis of what's eating your week."
			noindex={true}
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main class="ws">
			<section class="ws-hero">
				<p class="ws-eyebrow">Live workshop · 3 hours</p>
				<h1>Your team is drowning in manual work — bring one of those workflows and leave with a diagnosis.</h1>
				<p class="ws-sub">
					A 3-hour live working session on the OpenClaw setup I actually run in production.
					You'll watch it run on real problems, apply it to your own messiest process, and walk out
					with a <strong>named diagnosis</strong> of what's eating your week. Not a slide deck.
				</p>
				<p class="ws-sub ws-sub-note">
					It runs on a Saturday morning for one reason: it's the one block where nobody else's
					calendar gets a vote.
				</p>
				<ul class="ws-facts">
					<li><span>Format</span>3 hours, live, interactive</li>
					<li><span>Where</span>Zoom — link on confirmation</li>
					<li><span>When</span>{SESSION_DATE}</li>
					<li><span>Room</span>{SEAT_CAP}</li>
				</ul>
				<div class="ws-cta-row">
					<a class="ws-btn" href={CHECKOUT_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Get my seat — {EARLY_PRICE}</a>
					<span class="ws-cta-note">Early bird {EARLY_PRICE} · <s>{FULL_PRICE}</s> after</span>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="ws-section">
				<h2>The problem this is for</h2>
				<p>
					You're hiring for a role that is really a backlog. Support tickets, onboarding steps,
					data entry, ops reporting, compliance chasing — work that a person is doing by hand today
					because nobody has built the system that removes it. A hire is $60–100K a year; most of
					that backlog is automatable now.
				</p>
				<p>
					The blocker isn't information — there's more AI content than anyone can read. It's that
					you've never seen a real setup running on work like yours, and you don't know which of
					your processes is worth fixing first.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="ws-section">
				<h2>What you'll actually do</h2>
				<p>
					Five blocks: <strong>20 minutes teaching, 20 minutes applying it to your own business,
					10 minutes of me reviewing your work.</strong> The review is the point — it's where you
					find out what's actually wrong with your setup, not a generic version of it.
				</p>
				<table class="ws-agenda">
					<tbody>
						<tr><td class="n">0:00–0:20</td><td>How an agent actually runs real work — the setup, in plain terms.</td></tr>
						<tr><td class="n">0:20–0:40</td><td>You map your messiest manual workflow, live.</td></tr>
						<tr><td class="n">0:40–0:50</td><td>Review: I read your workflow back and name the bottleneck.</td></tr>
						<tr><td class="n">0:50–1:50</td><td>Repeat ×2 — the same loop on two more processes.</td></tr>
						<tr><td class="n">1:50–3:00</td><td>Live build-along + open review on attendee stacks.</td></tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
				<p class="ws-note">
					<strong>Come with:</strong> your messiest manual workflow. Describe it in a few lines —
					who does it, how often, what breaks. You'll leave with a diagnosis you can act on
					whether or not you ever pay me anything else.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="ws-section">
				<h2>Why this isn't free</h2>
				<p>
					Everything I'll teach is written down somewhere, for free. What isn't free is watching a
					real production setup get applied to <em>your</em> problem, live, with someone telling you
					which part is actually broken. That's the whole product.
				</p>
				<p>
					I'll be running my own environment on-screen the entire time — the one I use daily — so you
					can see exactly what "working" looks like, settings and all. No stock demos, no slideware.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="ws-section">
				<h2>Who this is for</h2>
				<div class="ws-cols">
					<div class="ws-for">
						<h3>It's for you if</h3>
						<ul>
							<li>You run a 10–30 person company and still touch operations yourself.</li>
							<li>You have a specific process that eats hours every week.</li>
							<li>You want to see it done, not read about it.</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
					<div class="ws-not">
						<h3>It isn't for you if</h3>
						<ul>
							<li>You want a course you can watch later and never apply.</li>
							<li>You're looking for enterprise procurement or a big-company rollout.</li>
							<li>You've already got a working agent stack you're happy with.</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="ws-section">
				<h2>Questions</h2>
				<dl class="ws-faq">
					<dt>Do I need to be technical?</dt>
					<dd>No. If you can describe the workflow in plain English, you can participate. I'll keep the build-along at a level you can follow.</dd>
					<dt>How do I pay?</dt>
				<dd>Card, Apple Pay, or Google Pay through Stripe's secure checkout. You'll get a receipt by email straight away.</dd>
				<dt>Is it recorded?</dt>
					<dd>Yes — registrants get the replay, so you can go back over anything. But come live: the review blocks are the product, and a replay can't review <em>your</em> workflow.</dd>
					<dt>What if the date doesn't work?</dt>
					<dd>Two options. Every seat is transferable to a future session, and {WEEKDAY_FALLBACK} Reply to your confirmation email and say so.</dd>
					<dt>What if not enough people sign up?</dt>
					<dd>{MIN_SEATS}</dd>
					<dt>What do I get for the money?</dt>
					<dd>The live session, the diagnosis of your own workflow, and everything I demonstrate. There's no upsell you have to buy to make the session useful.</dd>
				</dl>
			</section>

			<section class="ws-section ws-reserve" id="reserve">
				<h2>Reserve a seat</h2>
				<p class="ws-price"><span class="ws-amount">{EARLY_PRICE}</span> <span class="ws-was">early bird · {FULL_PRICE} after</span></p>
				<p>
					Three hours, live, {SEAT_CAP.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + SEAT_CAP.slice(1)}.
					Grab a seat and your Zoom link and session details land in your inbox straight away.
				</p>
				<div class="ws-cta-row">
					<a class="ws-btn" href={CHECKOUT_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Get my seat — {EARLY_PRICE}</a>
					<span class="ws-cta-note">Secure checkout · Card, Apple Pay &amp; Google Pay</span>
				</div>
				<p class="ws-fine">Seats are transferable to a future session — just reply to your confirmation email. {WEEKDAY_FALLBACK} The session runs with at least 5 paid seats; if it doesn't fill, you get a full refund or a transfer.</p>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.ws {
		max-width: 740px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 3rem 2.5rem 1rem;
	}
	.ws-hero {
		padding-bottom: 2rem;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
	}
	.ws-eyebrow {
		font-size: 0.8rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.14em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--color-accent);
		font-weight: 600;
		margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
	}
	.ws-hero h1 {
		font-family: var(--font-heading);
		font-size: 2.35rem;
		line-height: 1.2;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
	}
	.ws-sub {
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		color: var(--color-text-secondary);
		line-height: 1.7;
		margin: 0 0 1.6rem;
	}
	.ws-sub-note {
		font-size: 1rem;
		margin: -0.7rem 0 1.6rem;
		padding-left: 0.9rem;
		border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent-light);
	}
	.ws-facts {
		list-style: none;
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
		padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem;
		margin: 0 0 1.9rem;
		background: var(--color-bg-card);
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		border-radius: var(--border-radius);
	}
	.ws-facts li {
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		color: var(--color-text);
	}
	.ws-facts span {
		display: block;
		font-size: 0.72rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
		margin-bottom: 0.15rem;
	}
	.ws-cta-row {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 1rem;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
	}
	.ws-btn {
		display: inline-block;
		background: var(--color-accent);
		color: #fff;
		font-weight: 600;
		font-size: 1rem;
		padding: 0.85rem 1.5rem;
		border-radius: var(--border-radius);
		text-decoration: none;
	}
	.ws-btn:hover { background: var(--color-accent-hover); color: #fff; }
	.ws-cta-note { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
	.ws-cta-note s { color: var(--color-text-muted); }
	.ws-section { padding: 2.2rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-light); }
	.ws-section:last-of-type { border-bottom: none; }
	.ws h2 {
		font-family: var(--font-heading);
		font-size: 1.5rem;
		letter-spacing: -0.01em;
		margin: 0 0 0.8rem;
		border: none;
		padding: 0;
	}
	.ws h3 { font-size: 1rem; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
	.ws p { margin: 0 0 0.9rem; }
	.ws-agenda {
		width: 100%;
		border-collapse: collapse;
		margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
		font-size: 0.95rem;
	}
	.ws-agenda td {
		padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-light);
		vertical-align: top;
	}
	.ws-agenda .n {
		white-space: nowrap;
		color: var(--color-text-secondary);
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
		width: 8.5rem;
	}
	.ws-note {
		background: var(--color-accent-light);
		border-radius: var(--border-radius);
		padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem;
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		margin: 0;
	}
	.ws-cols { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; }
	.ws-cols ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; }
	.ws-cols li { font-size: 0.95rem; margin: 0.35rem 0; }
	.ws-for h3 { color: var(--color-accent); }
	.ws-not h3 { color: var(--color-text-muted); }
	.ws-faq dt { font-weight: 600; margin-top: 1rem; }
	.ws-faq dd { margin: 0.3rem 0 0; color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: 0.98rem; }
	.ws-reserve { padding-top: 2.4rem; }
	.ws-price { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.6rem; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
	.ws-amount { font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 2.2rem; font-weight: 600; }
	.ws-was { color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; }
	.ws-form label {
		display: block;
		font-size: 0.8rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
		margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
	}
	.ws-fields { display: flex; gap: 0.6rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
	.ws-fields input[type='email'] {
		flex: 1 1 16rem;
		min-width: 0;
		padding: 0.8rem 0.9rem;
		font: inherit;
		font-size: 1rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		border-radius: var(--border-radius);
		background: var(--color-bg-card);
		color: var(--color-text);
	}
	.ws-fields button {
		padding: 0.8rem 1.4rem;
		font: inherit;
		font-size: 1rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		color: #fff;
		background: var(--color-accent);
		border: none;
		border-radius: var(--border-radius);
		cursor: pointer;
	}
	.ws-fields button:hover { background: var(--color-accent-hover); }
	.ws-fine { font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); margin: 0.7rem 0 0; }
	@media (max-width: 620px) {
		.ws { padding: 2rem 1.25rem 0.5rem; }
		.ws-hero h1 { font-size: 1.85rem; }
		.ws-facts { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
		.ws-cols { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
		.ws-fields button { flex: 1 1 100%; }
		.ws-agenda, .ws-agenda tbody, .ws-agenda tr, .ws-agenda td { display: block; width: auto; }
		.ws-agenda tr { padding: 0.6rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-light); }
		.ws-agenda td { border: none; padding: 0; }
		.ws-agenda .n { font-size: 0.78rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--color-text-muted); margin-bottom: 0.15rem; }
	}
</style>
